-- ops_liveness_registry reseeded so it lists WAVE 3's first three alongside every platform already
-- in it: wahadat, squares, rawaf. 119 platforms -> 122.
--
-- WHY A FULL RESEED AND NOT THREE INSERTS: verify-liveness-registry-mirror holds THREE things to
-- the same content — scrapers/common/liveness_policies.py, sql/mirrors/liveness_registry.json and
-- the newest reseed migration's own seed — and it also requires the delete clause below, because
-- an insert-only seed cannot RETIRE a platform and the coverage dashboard would go on reporting
-- verification for inventory nothing checks any more. All three were regenerated from the Python
-- registry in one pass, so they agree by construction rather than by hand-editing three files.
--
-- ALL THREE ARE CRAWL_PRESENCE_ONLY, AND THAT IS A CORRECTION. They were first registered
-- CANDIDATE_PLUS_DIRECT, which asserts that something re-fetches each listing's own URL and records
-- an affirmative answer. No such code was written for any of them, and
-- verify-liveness-registry-mirror caught the overclaim: it would have reported 100% verified while
-- verifying nothing. Each is now declared in scrapers/absence-only-prune.txt (ratchet 24 -> 27)
-- with the route to upgrade it written down:
--   wahadat — no oracle is POSSIBLE: the per-unit endpoint on pro.wahadat.sa answers 403
--             unauthenticated, so a "direct" check would only re-read the project page the crawl
--             just read and dress a presence signal up as a second opinion.
--   squares — an oracle IS possible (every post has a real /property/<slug>/ URL); simply not
--             written yet. The catalogue is complete and self-declaring (X-WP-Total=18 matched 18).
--   rawaf   — an oracle is easy (re-read the unit's own status from /api/deals/<projectId>, where
--             the source itself says SOLD); not written yet. run.py additionally suppresses
--             prune_unseen entirely whenever any project failed to serve its units, so a partial
--             sweep can never retire live stock.
